{"text": "UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA, MERCED\nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC SAFETY\n\nPolice Services, Emergency Management, Violence Prevention\n\nMEMORANDUM\nDate: November 26, 2015\n\nTO: Lt. Kevin MeNiff\nFROM: Officer Brandon Thomas\nSUBJECT: Request for Investigative Information\n\nLt. MeNiff, in regards to your email received 11-24-2015, I have attached Officer\nLopea\u2019s (UCMPD 434) range records prior to 11-04-2015. Officer Lopez\u2019s Sig Sauer pistol was\ninspected prior to being issued. The pistol was issued without modification or mechanical\ndefects. The ammo issued to Officer Lopez is 185 grain HST Federal Premium, caliber .40\nS&W.\n= ~ After the O18, Officer Lopez's firearm was collected by myself and turned over to the\nMerced County Sheriff's Officer for their investigation. Officer Lopez placed the gun himself\ninto an evidence box, and it was secured in the armory until being turned over. At no time was\nthe gun inspected or manipulated by myself or any other UCMPD staff prior to being taken as\n\nevidence,\n\n\u2014 7\n\nUC Merced Police Department\n5200 N. Lake Rd.\nMerced, CA 95340",
